message: "If you use this work, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "A sharp smoothing inequality in Gauss space and the exact threshold for local entropy concavity"
abstract: "Unrefereed research candidate. Near the Gaussian, the entropy of a noisy mixture of two copies of a symmetric signal is concave in the mixing weight exactly when the signal fraction is at most 4/7 (total signal-to-noise ratio 4/3); with three or more copies, concavity on the whole simplex of weights fails at every signal fraction. The proof rests on a sharp smoothing inequality for bounded functions in Gauss space."
